---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DownloadButtons from "../components/DownloadButtons.astro";
import { formatDate, getReleases } from "../lib/releases";
import { site } from "../site.config.mjs";

const releases = await getReleases();
const latest = releases[0];
---

<Base title="Download" description="Download Drift for Windows or macOS, or try it in your browser.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
    <h1>Get Drift</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Free for Windows and macOS, or open it in your browser with nothing to install.{" "}
      {
        latest && (
          <>
            The newest version is <strong>{latest.version}</strong>, released{" "}
            {formatDate(latest.published)}.
          </>
        )
      }
    </p>

    <div class="card dl">
      <DownloadButtons />
    </div>

    <div class="notes">
      <section>
        <h2>Drift is alpha software</h2>
        <p>
          It works, and testers use it for real drawings, but expect rough edges and save often.
          A file saved by a newer Drift won't open in an older one, so if you share drawings,
          everyone should use the same version. Drift tells you when an update is ready.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>The first time you open it</h2>
        <p>Drift isn't code-signed yet, so your computer asks before opening it the first time.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Windows:</strong> if SmartScreen says "Windows protected your PC", choose
            <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>macOS:</strong> open the disk image and drag Drift to Applications. The first
            time, Control-click Drift and choose <em>Open</em>, or allow it in
            <em>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</em>.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Updates installed from inside Drift don't ask again.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Checking a download</h2>
        <p>
          Each release lists SHA-256 checksums in <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code>, signed with Drift's
          release key. Older versions and checksums are on the{" "}
          <a href={`${site.repoUrl}/releases`}>GitHub releases page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: 56px;
  }
  .dl {
    margin: 32px 0 56px;
    padding: 32px;
  }
  .notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 32px;
    color: var(--text-weak);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .notes h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .notes strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .dl {
      padding: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
